					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-234462#post-3810334</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-234462/scp-192#post-3810334</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 23 May 2018 16:17:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>wishun</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1204404</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>If this was a camera it would be a worn out cliché; pretty sure there is a Goosebumps book about that. Spinning it as a more obscure imaging device helps, but not enough.</p> <p>I like that the researchers pinned it down to the specific component (as opposed to assuming the whole machine was anomalous), which puts me at neutral vote</p> <p>What tipped it to negative was the extended discussion of transfer and procedure revisions, as if dealing with this was a major project. Put it in a lead box, put the box in a locked room, treat it like any other radioactive material, 'nuff said.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-234462#post-3737970</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
